{"title":"Career roadmap — Patient Relations Officer","role":"Patient Relations Officer","summary":"A Patient Relations Officer (PRO) acts as a bridge between patients, families, doctors, nurses, hospital administration, billing, insurance, and support departments. The role focuses on patient experience, communication, grievance resolution, service coordination, feedback, and hospital operations.","facts":{"Current degree":"BBA / BMS / BBM (Bachelor of Business Administration / Management Studies)","Course":"BBA – Hospital / Healthcare Management"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"For a BBA Healthcare Management graduate, the strongest route is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Healthcare operations","patient communication","hospital systems","service quality","insurance/billing basics","healthcare analytics"],"sep":"+"}]},{"heading":"Career horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Patient Relations Executive / Patient Relations Officer; build patient-service, hospital workflow and grievance-management skills"}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Senior Patient Relations Officer / Patient Experience Specialist / Hospital Operations Executive"}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Patient Experience Manager / Hospital Operations Manager / Service Quality Manager"}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Head of Patient Experience / Hospital Administration Leader / Healthcare Operations Director"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to build each year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Healthcare + management foundations"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Principles of management"},{"text":"Healthcare management"},{"text":"Hospital organisation"},{"text":"Healthcare economics"},{"text":"Business communication"},{"text":"Organisational behaviour"},{"text":"Basic accounting"},{"text":"Healthc